 running on, and an UPDATE which works on at-least 1.2 and 1.3 branches failed.  This error was inconsistent with the behavior expected in https://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/14/changelog/changelog_14.html#change-f413ff8c13a1fb7d766bfa16dfcdfbf1 ; I believe this may be linked to #4617.  However, I think this exception is more likely due to me mixing the ORM and core in a way that worked (was it supposed to?), but no longer does (is it supposed to?).\r\n\r\nSqlAlchemy raises an Exception:\r\n\r\n    AttributeError: 'Subquery' object has no attribute 'as_scalar'\r\n\r\nLooking at the migration guide though, I tried the new API and...\r\n\r\n    AttributeError: 'Subquery' object has no attribute 'scalar_subquery'\r\n\r\nThe code to illustrate below, I can generate a test case to reproduce if need.\r\n\r\n```\r\n    _q_sub = (\r\n        dbSession.query(models.MyTable.id)\r\n            .order_by(models.MyTable.id.desc())\r\n            .limit(1)\r\n            .subquery()\r\n            .as_scalar()  # also fails as `.scalar_subquery()`\r\n    )\r\n    dbSession.execute(\r\n        models.MyTable2.__table__.update().values(\r\n            mytable_id=_q_sub\r\n        )\r\n    )\r\n```","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","even